{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788460210259,"sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bc64849171c9d4c3","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/runtime/toylang.c","limit":60,"offset":1190},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/runtime/toylang.c</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1190:  * is what tells Int (32-bit wrap after every addition) from Int64 (none). Accumulated in\n1191:  * uint64_t so no addition can overflow into undefined behaviour; the narrow step truncates to\n1192:  * 32 bits and sign-extends. */\n1193: int64_t tl_vec_sum(const tl_vec *v, int narrow) {\n1194:     uint64_t acc = 0;\n1195:     for (int64_t i = 0; i < v->len; i++) {\n1196:         acc += (uint64_t)v->cols[0][i];\n1197:         if (narrow) {\n1198:             acc = (uint64_t)(int64_t)(int32_t)acc;\n1199:         }\n1200:     }\n1201:     return (int64_t)acc;\n1202: }\n1203: \n1204: /* `max` over a Vec of Int or Int64: the greatest raw slot, Int's already sign-extended so the\n1205:  * i64 comparison orders it correctly. NULL on an empty Vec, the same absence encoding\n1206:  * tl_opt_some uses everywhere else, so a caller unwraps it the way it unwraps an Index result. */\n1207: int64_t *tl_vec_max(const tl_vec *v) {\n1208:     if (v->len == 0) {\n1209:         return NULL;\n1210:     }\n1211:     int64_t m = v->cols[0][0];\n1212:     for (int64_t i = 1; i < v->len; i++) {\n1213:         if (v->cols[0][i] > m) {\n1214:             m = v->cols[0][i];\n1215:         }\n1216:     }\n1217:     return tl_opt_some(m);\n1218: }\n1219: \n1220: /* Collapse one dimension at `i`, `depth` layers down, counting from the end when negative.\n1221:  *\n1222:  * `is_record` decides whether an entry has to be gathered out of the columns. The column count\n1223:  * cannot stand in for that test: a record with one field has