{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788460367530,"sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-b31521eb08c412c6","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/tir.rs","newString":"    /// `max(v)`, the greatest of `v`'s elements, `Opt<T>` because an empty Vec has no maximum\n    /// -- the same answer indexing gives to absence (kantord/toylang#140). Restricted to the\n    /// same two integer element types `sum` takes, so a backend can reach for its native\n    /// maximum.\n    Max,\n    /// `first(v)`, the first element of a Vec, `Opt<T>` because an empty Vec has none. The cut\n    /// operator of the query-is-search model (draft.md#query-is-search, gh:142): a reified\n    /// search is a `Vec`, and `first` commits to the first answer, abandoning the rest. Over a\n    /// Stream the same operation is an early exit on the first element, which is the\n    /// lazy/unbounded case the model opens the door to and this row does not yet reach.\n    First,\n    /// `any(v)`, whether any element of a `Vec<Bool>` is true; an empty Vec is false. The\n    /// existential cut of the same model: a `Vec<Bool>` is a reified search reduced to a mask,\n    /// and `any` is whether the mask is set anywhere.\n    Any,\n    /// `all(v)`, whether every element of a `Vec<Bool>` is true; an empty Vec is true (vacuous,\n    /// the same answer `reduce`'s identity gives). The universal cut, `any`'s dual.\n    All,\n}","oldString":"    /// `max(v)`, the greatest of `v`'s elements, `Opt<T>` because an empty Vec has no maximum\n    /// -- the same answer indexing gives to absence (kantord/toylang#140). Restricted to the\n    /// same two integer element types `sum` takes, so a backend can reach for its native\n    /// maximum.\n    Max,\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/tir.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/tir.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/tir.rs\n@@ -255,8 +255,21 @@\n     /// -- the same answer indexing gives to absence (kantord/toylang#140). Restricted to the\n     /// same two integer element types `sum` takes, so a backend can reach for its native\n     /// maximum.\n     Max,\n+    /// `first(v)`, the first element of a Vec, `Opt<T>` because an empty Vec has none. The cut\n+    /// operator of the query-is-search model (draft.md#query-is-search, gh:142): a reified\n+    /// search is a `Vec`, and `first` commits to the first answer, abandoning the rest. Over a\n+    /// Stream the same operation is an early exit on the first element, which is the\n+    /// lazy/unbounded case the model opens the door to and this row does not yet reach.\n+    First,\n+    /// `any(v)`, whether any element of a `Vec<Bool>` is true; an empty Vec is false. The\n+    /// existential cut of the same model: a `Vec<Bool>` is a reified search reduced to a mask,\n+    /// and `any` is whether the mask is set anywhere.\n+    Any,\n+    /// `all(v)`, whether every element of a `Vec<Bool>` is true; an empty Vec is true (vacuous,\n+    /// the same answer `reduce`'s identity gives). The universal cut, `any`'s dual.\n+    All,\n }\n \n pub struct Func {\n     pub name: String,\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/tir.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/tir.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/tir.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/tir.rs\n@@ -255,8 +255,21 @@\n     /// -- the same answer indexing gives to absence (kantord/toylang#140). Restricted to the\n     /// same two integer element types `sum` takes, so a backend can reach for its native\n     /// maximum.\n     Max,\n+    /// `first(v)`, the first element of a Vec, `Opt<T>` because an empty Vec has none. The cut\n+    /// operator of the query-is-search model (draft.md#query-is-search, gh:142): a reified\n+    /// search is a `Vec`, and `first` commits to the first answer, abandoning the rest. Over a\n+    /// Stream the same operation is an early exit on the first element, which is the\n+    /// lazy/unbounded case the model opens the door to and this row does not yet reach.\n+    First,\n+    /// `any(v)`, whether any element of a `Vec<Bool>` is true; an empty Vec is false. The\n+    /// existential cut of the same model: a `Vec<Bool>` is a reified search reduced to a mask,\n+    /// and `any` is whether the mask is set anywhere.\n+    Any,\n+    /// `all(v)`, whether every element of a `Vec<Bool>` is true; an empty Vec is true (vacuous,\n+    /// the same answer `reduce`'s identity gives). The universal cut, `any`'s dual.\n+    All,\n }\n \n pub struct Func {\n     pub name: String,\n","additions":13,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/tir.rs","time":{"start":1788460367527,"end":1788460367529}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Let me start with the TIR. Add `First`, `Any`, `All` to the `Builtin` enum. The `Builtin` enum has `#[derive(Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]`. I'll add the three variants after `Max`, with doc comments.\n\nDesign decision for the comments:\n- `First`: `first(v)`, the first element of a Vec, `Opt<T>` because an empty Vec has no first -- the cut operator of the query-is-search model (gh:142). Like `max` returns `Opt<T>` for the same absence reason, and over a Stream it is the early-exit the door is opened to.\n- `Any`: `any(v)`, whether any element of a `Vec<Bool>` is true. Empty -> false.\n- `All`: `all(v)`, whether every element of a `Vec<Bool>` is true. Empty -> true (vacuous).\n\nLet me add them.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0688b6a41001ljiXT8HQeakLpZ","sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","messageID":"msg_0688b5623001RcQg3MeDEGf8AX"}}
