{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788460408733,"sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bade41e51b9b5947","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_js.rs","newString":"// `>` orders Number and BigInt alike, so one maximum serves both widths.\nconst MAX_HELPER: &str = \"\\\nfunction tl_max(v) {\n  if (v.length === 0) return \\\"none\\\";\n  let m = v[0];\n  for (let i = 1; i < v.length; i++) if (v[i] > m) m = v[i];\n  return { some: m };\n}\n\";\n\n// The cut operator of the query-is-search model (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first`\n// commits to the first answer. An empty Vec has no first, so the absent Opt is tagged the way\n// `tl_max` tags it.\nconst FIRST_HELPER: &str = \"\\\nfunction tl_first(v) {\n  if (v.length === 0) return \\\"none\\\";\n  return { some: v[0] };\n}\n\";\n","oldString":"// `>` orders Number and BigInt alike, so one maximum serves both widths.\nconst MAX_HELPER: &str = \"\\\nfunction tl_max(v) {\n  if (v.length === 0) return \\\"none\\\";\n  let m = v[0];\n  for (let i = 1; i < v.length; i++) if (v[i] > m) m = v[i];\n  return { some: m };\n}\n\";\n"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_js.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_js.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_js.rs\n@@ -191,8 +191,18 @@\n   return { some: m };\n }\n \";\n \n+// The cut operator of the query-is-search model (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first`\n+// commits to the first answer. An empty Vec has no first, so the absent Opt is tagged the way\n+// `tl_max` tags it.\n+const FIRST_HELPER: &str = \"\\\n+function tl_first(v) {\n+  if (v.length === 0) return \\\"none\\\";\n+  return { some: v[0] };\n+}\n+\";\n+\n pub fn emit(program: &Program) -> String {\n     let enums = &program.enums;\n     let mut out = String::new();\n \n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_js.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_js.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_js.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_js.rs\n@@ -191,8 +191,18 @@\n   return { some: m };\n }\n \";\n \n+// The cut operator of the query-is-search model (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first`\n+// commits to the first answer. An empty Vec has no first, so the absent Opt is tagged the way\n+// `tl_max` tags it.\n+const FIRST_HELPER: &str = \"\\\n+function tl_first(v) {\n+  if (v.length === 0) return \\\"none\\\";\n+  return { some: v[0] };\n+}\n+\";\n+\n pub fn emit(program: &Program) -> String {\n     let enums = &program.enums;\n     let mut out = String::new();\n \n","additions":10,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/emit_js.rs","time":{"start":1788460408726,"end":1788460408731}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now the emitters. Let me start with the JS emitter. I need to:\n1. Add `FIRST_HELPER` const (`tl_first`).\n2. Add `first: bool` to `Helpers`.\n3. Set `used.first |= *which == Builtin::First;` in the walk. (any/all are inlined, no helper, so no tracking needed -- but let me double check that `any`/`all` over `Vec<Bool>` need no helper. JS `.some`/`.every` are native, so inline. No tracking.)\n4. Add `(used.first, FIRST_HELPER)` to the dispatch.\n5. Add `Builtin::First`/`Any`/`All` arms in `expr`.\n\nFor `first`, the helper:\n```js\nfunction tl_first(v) {\n  if (v.length === 0) return \"none\";\n  return { some: v[0] };\n}\n```\n\nFor `any`: `format!(\"({}).some(x => x)\", expr(...))`. For `all`: `format!(\"({}).every(x => x)\", expr(...))`.\n\nWait -- but the element of a `Vec<Bool>` is a JS boolean `true`/`false`. `[true, false].some(x => x)` = true. Good. `[true, false].every(x => x)` = false. Good. Empty: `[].some(...)` = false, `[].every(...)` = true. \n\nLet me write the JS changes. First the helper const after MAX_HELPER.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0688c14e6001gUocgmj42epNq8","sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","messageID":"msg_0688c0129001uIUWOKvIxBLTzW"}}
