{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788460446551,"sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-9d76b389bd5804db","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_jq.rs","newString":"            // jq's own `max` on an empty list errors, and on a non-empty one is exactly this,\n            // so only the empty case is spelled: the absent Opt, tagged the way `Tail` tags.\n            Builtin::Max => format!(\n                \"({} | if length == 0 then \\\"none\\\" else {{some: max}} end)\",\n                expr(enums, arg)\n            ),\n            // The cut operator (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first` commits to the\n            // first answer. `.[0]` on an empty array is `null` rather than the tagged absence\n            // `Opt` promises, so both cases are spelled the way `Tail`/`max` spell them.\n            Builtin::First => format!(\n                \"({} | if length == 0 then \\\"none\\\" else {{some: .[0]}} end)\",\n                expr(enums, arg)\n            ),\n            // jq's own `any`/`all` over a `Vec<Bool>` are exactly the existential/universal cuts\n            // of the model: empty is false for `any`, true for `all` (vacuous), and both\n            // short-circuit the way the cuts do.\n            Builtin::Any => format!(\"({} | any)\", expr(enums, arg)),\n            Builtin::All => format!(\"({} | all)\", expr(enums, arg)),","oldString":"            // jq's own `max` on an empty list errors, and on a non-empty one is exactly this,\n            // so only the empty case is spelled: the absent Opt, tagged the way `Tail` tags.\n            Builtin::Max => format!(\n                \"({} | if length == 0 then \\\"none\\\" else {{some: max}} end)\",\n                expr(enums, arg)\n            ),"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_jq.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_jq.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_jq.rs\n@@ -581,8 +581,20 @@\n Builtin::Max => format!(\n     \"({} | if length == 0 then \\\"none\\\" else {{some: max}} end)\",\n     expr(enums, arg)\n ),\n+// The cut operator (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first` commits to the\n+// first answer. `.[0]` on an empty array is `null` rather than the tagged absence\n+// `Opt` promises, so both cases are spelled the way `Tail`/`max` spell them.\n+Builtin::First => format!(\n+    \"({} | if length == 0 then \\\"none\\\" else {{some: .[0]}} end)\",\n+    expr(enums, arg)\n+),\n+// jq's own `any`/`all` over a `Vec<Bool>` are exactly the existential/universal cuts\n+// of the model: empty is false for `any`, true for `all` (vacuous), and both\n+// short-circuit the way the cuts do.\n+Builtin::Any => format!(\"({} | any)\", expr(enums, arg)),\n+Builtin::All => format!(\"({} | all)\", expr(enums, arg)),\n // The names come from the checked type, not the object value, so `arg` runs only to\n // become the `.` a literal array then ignores -- the same discard the pipe already\n // gives every other builtin here.\n Builtin::Fields => {\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_jq.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_jq.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_jq.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_jq.rs\n@@ -581,8 +581,20 @@\n Builtin::Max => format!(\n     \"({} | if length == 0 then \\\"none\\\" else {{some: max}} end)\",\n     expr(enums, arg)\n ),\n+// The cut operator (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first` commits to the\n+// first answer. `.[0]` on an empty array is `null` rather than the tagged absence\n+// `Opt` promises, so both cases are spelled the way `Tail`/`max` spell them.\n+Builtin::First => format!(\n+    \"({} | if length == 0 then \\\"none\\\" else {{some: .[0]}} end)\",\n+    expr(enums, arg)\n+),\n+// jq's own `any`/`all` over a `Vec<Bool>` are exactly the existential/universal cuts\n+// of the model: empty is false for `any`, true for `all` (vacuous), and both\n+// short-circuit the way the cuts do.\n+Builtin::Any => format!(\"({} | any)\", expr(enums, arg)),\n+Builtin::All => format!(\"({} | all)\", expr(enums, arg)),\n // The names come from the checked type, not the object value, so `arg` runs only to\n // become the `.` a literal array then ignores -- the same discard the pipe already\n // gives every other builtin here.\n Builtin::Fields => {\n","additions":12,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/emit_jq.rs","time":{"start":1788460446547,"end":1788460446550}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now the jq emitter. Add `First`/`Any`/`All` arms after `Max`. For jq:\n- `first`: `({} | if length == 0 then \"none\" else {some: .[0]} end)`.\n- `any`: `({} | any)` -- jq's `any` with no filter. But wait, the elements are booleans `true`/`false`. `any` over an array of booleans: `[true, false] | any` = true. But actually jq's `any` is `any(g)` -- when called with no argument, it's `any(.[])`. Hmm, actually I need to verify. In jq, `any` is defined as `any(generator; condition)` or `any(condition)` where `condition` is applied to `.`. Let me think. `any` with zero arguments: `any` is `any(.[])`? No. Actually jq's `any/0` is defined as `any(.[])` -- it returns true if any element of the input array is truthy. Let me verify: from jq manual, `any` takes no args and is \"true if any element of the input array is truthy\". Actually the jq builtin `any` is `any(g)` or `any(g; c)`. `any/0` is `any(.[])`. So `[true, false] | any` -> true, `[] | any` -> false, `[false] | any` -> false. Good.\n\nWait, actually I'm not 100% sure `any/0` iterates the array. Let me reconsider. In jq, `any` (zero args) is defined as `any(.[])`? Or is it `any(.)` meaning \"is . truthy\"? Hmm. Let me think about what jq actually does. The jq manual says: `any`, `all` -- \"The filter `any` outputs `true` if any element of the input array is truthy.\" Actually the precise definition: `any` is `reduce .[] as $x (false; . or $x)` essentially, or `any(.[])`. So over `[true, false]` it yields true. Over `[]` it yields false. Good.\n\nBut actually, wait -- there's a subtlety. The jq manual defines `any` as: \"Outputs true if the input is truthy, or if any element of the input array is truthy.\" No. Let me just be safe and use `any(.[])` explicitly, or `reduce`. Actually the cleanest and most certain: `({} | reduce .[] as $x (false; . or $x))` for any, `({} | reduce .[] as $x (true; . and $x))` for all. But that's verbose. Let me check what jq's `any`/`all` zero-arg actually does.\n\nFrom the jq manual (1.7): \n- `any` / `any(generator)` / `any(generator; condition)`: \"The two-argument ... The one-argument form ... The zero-argument form ... `any` outputs `true` if any output of the input stream is truthy.\" Hmm, \"input stream\" -- when the input is an array `[true, false]`, `.[]` streams `true`, `false`, and `any` checks if any is truthy -> true.\n\nActually, the zero-arg `any` is `any(.[])`. So `[true, false] | any` = true. Good. And `all` zero-arg is `all(.[])`. `[true, false] | all` = false, `[] | all` = true (vacuous -- `all` over empty stream is true). Good.\n\nSo:\n- `any`: `format!(\"({} | any)\", expr(enums, arg))`.\n- `all`: `format!(\"({} | all)\", expr(enums, arg))`.\n\nBut wait, I want to be careful. The element values are `true`/`false` (booleans). `any` checks truthiness. `true` is truthy, `false` is falsy. So `[true, false] | any` = true. `[false] | any` = false. `[] | any` = false. `[true] | all` = true. `[true, false] | all` = false. `[] | all` = true. \n\nLet me use the zero-arg forms. They're clean and match the model.\n\nFor `first`: `format!(\"({} | if length == 0 then \\\"none\\\" else {{some: .[0]}} end)\", expr(enums, arg))`.\n\nLet me add the jq arms.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0688c9952001bcSZ1KFRDyvo4a","sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","messageID":"msg_0688c5dac001SL92HOQ65Kh9Fl"}}
