{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788460514523,"sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a363da66c910a5ea","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_rs.rs","newString":"// `Option::max` is exactly the empty-is-absent answer, and `Ord` covers both integer widths.\nconst MAX_HELPER: &str = r#\"fn tl_max<T: Clone + Ord>(v: &[T]) -> Option<T> {\n    v.iter().cloned().max()\n}\n\"#;\n\n// The cut operator (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first` commits to the first answer.\n// `Option::first` is exactly the empty-is-absent answer, the same one `tl_max` reaches through\n// `max`.\nconst FIRST_HELPER: &str = r#\"fn tl_first<T: Clone>(v: &[T]) -> Option<T> {\n    v.first().cloned()\n}\n\"#;\n","oldString":"// `Option::max` is exactly the empty-is-absent answer, and `Ord` covers both integer widths.\nconst MAX_HELPER: &str = r#\"fn tl_max<T: Clone + Ord>(v: &[T]) -> Option<T> {\n    v.iter().cloned().max()\n}\n\"#;\n"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_rs.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_rs.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_rs.rs\n@@ -154,8 +154,16 @@\n     v.iter().cloned().max()\n }\n \"#;\n \n+// The cut operator (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first` commits to the first answer.\n+// `Option::first` is exactly the empty-is-absent answer, the same one `tl_max` reaches through\n+// `max`.\n+const FIRST_HELPER: &str = r#\"fn tl_first<T: Clone>(v: &[T]) -> Option<T> {\n+    v.first().cloned()\n+}\n+\"#;\n+\n const RANGE_HELPER: &str = r#\"fn tl_range(n: i32) -> Vec<i32> {\n     (0..n.max(0)).collect()\n }\n \"#;\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_rs.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_rs.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_rs.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_rs.rs\n@@ -154,8 +154,16 @@\n     v.iter().cloned().max()\n }\n \"#;\n \n+// The cut operator (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first` commits to the first answer.\n+// `Option::first` is exactly the empty-is-absent answer, the same one `tl_max` reaches through\n+// `max`.\n+const FIRST_HELPER: &str = r#\"fn tl_first<T: Clone>(v: &[T]) -> Option<T> {\n+    v.first().cloned()\n+}\n+\"#;\n+\n const RANGE_HELPER: &str = r#\"fn tl_range(n: i32) -> Vec<i32> {\n     (0..n.max(0)).collect()\n }\n \"#;\n","additions":8,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/emit_rs.rs","time":{"start":1788460514520,"end":1788460514522}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"`DERIVE = \"#[derive(Clone, PartialEq)]\"` -- records and enums derive `Clone`. So `tl_first<T: Clone>` works for any element type including records and enums.\n\nNow let me add the Rust `FIRST_HELPER` after `MAX_HELPER`, the dispatch entry, and the `expr` arms. For `any`/`all` I'll inline with `.iter().any(|x| *x)` / `.iter().all(|x| *x)`.\n\nWait, but for the Rust emitter, `self.expr(arg)` returns an expression. Let me look at how `Length` is emitted: `format!(\"(({}).len() as i32)\", self.expr(arg))`. So `({expr}).iter()...`. For a `Vec<bool>`, `({expr}).iter().any(|x| *x)`. Good.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: should I use a helper for `any`/`all` in Rust to keep it clean? `v.iter().any(|x| *x)` is idiomatic Rust and one line. Inline is fine. Let me inline.\n\nLet me add the FIRST_HELPER.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0688db438001Gz