{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788460533637,"sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-abd568466a58da74","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_go.rs","newString":"// `cmp.Ordered` covers both integer widths, so one helper serves Int and Int64. Absence is the\n// zero `tlOpt`, the same answer an out-of-range index gives.\nconst MAX_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlMax[T cmp.Ordered](v []T) tlOpt[T] {\n\tif len(v) == 0 {\n\t\treturn tlOpt[T]{}\n\t}\n\tm := v[0]\n\tfor _, x := range v[1:] {\n\t\tif x > m {\n\t\t\tm = x\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn tlOpt[T]{true, m}\n}\n\"#;\n\n// The cut operator (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first` commits to the first answer.\n// Absence is the zero `tlOpt`, the same answer `tlMax` gives an empty Vec.\nconst FIRST_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlFirst[T any](v []T) tlOpt[T] {\n\tif len(v) == 0 {\n\t\treturn tlOpt[T]{}\n\t}\n\treturn tlOpt[T]{true, v[0]}\n}\n\"#;\n\n// `any`/`all` reduce a `Vec<Bool>` to one Bool, the existential and universal cuts of the same\n// model. Go has no native spelling over a slice, so both are loops that short-circuit the way\n// the cuts do; empty is false for `any`, true for `all` (vacuous).\nconst ANY_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlAny(v []bool) bool {\n\tfor _, x := range v {\n\t\tif x {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n\"#;\n\nconst ALL_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlAll(v []bool) bool {\n\tfor _, x := range v {\n\t\tif !x {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}\n\"#;\n","oldString":"// `cmp.Ordered` covers both integer widths, so one helper serves Int and Int64. Absence is the\n// zero `tlOpt`, the same answer an out-of-range index gives.\nconst MAX_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlMax[T cmp.Ordered](v []T) tlOpt[T] {\n\tif len(v) == 0 {\n\t\treturn tlOpt[T]{}\n\t}\n\tm := v[0]\n\tfor _, x := range v[1:] {\n\t\tif x > m {\n\t\t\tm = x\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn tlOpt[T]{true, m}\n}\n\"#;\n"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_go.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_go.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_go.rs\n@@ -178,8 +178,41 @@\n \treturn tlOpt[T]{true, m}\n }\n \"#;\n \n+// The cut operator (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first` commits to the first answer.\n+// Absence is the zero `tlOpt`, the same answer `tlMax` gives an empty Vec.\n+const FIRST_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlFirst[T any](v []T) tlOpt[T] {\n+\tif len(v) == 0 {\n+\t\treturn tlOpt[T]{}\n+\t}\n+\treturn tlOpt[T]{true, v[0]}\n+}\n+\"#;\n+\n+// `any`/`all` reduce a `Vec<Bool>` to one Bool, the existential and universal cuts of the same\n+// model. Go has no native spelling over a slice, so both are loops that short-circuit the way\n+// the cuts do; empty is false for `any`, true for `all` (vacuous).\n+const ANY_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlAny(v []bool) bool {\n+\tfor _, x := range v {\n+\t\tif x {\n+\t\t\treturn true\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn false\n+}\n+\"#;\n+\n+const ALL_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlAll(v []bool) bool {\n+\tfor _, x := range v {\n+\t\tif !x {\n+\t\t\treturn false\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn true\n+}\n+\"#;\n+\n /// Go's `int32` wraps on overflow by definition, and its `/` and `%` truncate toward zero, so\n /// only the zero divisor needs a guard. `MIN / -1` is defined to be `MIN` here, which is the\n /// wrapping answer the other backends were made to give.\n const ARITH_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlDiv(a, b int32) int32 {\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_go.rs","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_go.rs\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_go.rs\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_go.rs\n@@ -178,8 +178,41 @@\n \treturn tlOpt[T]{true, m}\n }\n \"#;\n \n+// The cut operator (gh:142): a reified search is a Vec, and `first` commits to the first answer.\n+// Absence is the zero `tlOpt`, the same answer `tlMax` gives an empty Vec.\n+const FIRST_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlFirst[T any](v []T) tlOpt[T] {\n+\tif len(v) == 0 {\n+\t\treturn tlOpt[T]{}\n+\t}\n+\treturn tlOpt[T]{true, v[0]}\n+}\n+\"#;\n+\n+// `any`/`all` reduce a `Vec<Bool>` to one Bool, the existential and universal cuts of the same\n+// model. Go has no native spelling over a slice, so both are loops that short-circuit the way\n+// the cuts do; empty is false for `any`, true for `all` (vacuous).\n+const ANY_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlAny(v []bool) bool {\n+\tfor _, x := range v {\n+\t\tif x {\n+\t\t\treturn true\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn false\n+}\n+\"#;\n+\n+const ALL_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlAll(v []bool) bool {\n+\tfor _, x := range v {\n+\t\tif !x {\n+\t\t\treturn false\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\treturn true\n+}\n+\"#;\n+\n /// Go's `int32` wraps on overflow by definition, and its `/` and `%` truncate toward zero, so\n /// only the zero divisor needs a guard. `MIN / -1` is defined to be `MIN` here, which is the\n /// wrapping answer the other backends were made to give.\n const ARITH_HELPER: &str = r#\"func tlDiv(a, b int32) int32 {\n","additions":33,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"src/emit_go.rs","time":{"start":1788460533633,"end":1788460533635}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"Now the Go emitter. Add `FIRST_HELPER` (`tlFirst`), `ANY_HELPER` (`tlAny`), `ALL_HELPER` (`tlAll`). Add to the dispatch, the walk's no-tracking arm, and the `expr` arms.\n\nGo Opt: `tlOpt[T]{}` (absent) / `tlOpt[T]{true, v}` (present).\n\n`tlFirst`:\n```go\nfunc tlFirst[T any](v []T) tlOpt[T] {\n\tif len(v) == 0 {\n\t\treturn tlOpt[T]{}\n\t}\n\treturn tlOpt[T]{true, v[0]}\n}\n```\n\n`tlAny`:\n```go\nfunc tlAny(v []bool) bool {\n\tfor _, x := range v {\n\t\tif x {\n\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn false\n}\n```\n\n`tlAll`:\n```go\nfunc tlAll(v []bool) bool {\n\tfor _, x := range v {\n\t\tif !x {\n\t\t\treturn false\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn true\n}\n```\n\nNow the dispatch: `(uses(\"tlFirst(\"), FIRST_HELPER)`, `(uses(\"tlAny(\"), ANY_HELPER)`, `(uses(\"tlAll(\"), ALL_HELPER)`. And the `tlOpt` gating: `if uses(\"tlOpt[\") || uses(\"tlAt(\") || uses(\"tlTail(\") || unwrap {` -- I need to add `uses(\"tlFirst(\")` to that condition since `tlFirst` returns `tlOpt[T]`. Let me update that line.\n\nAlso the walk's no-tracking arm at line 769-780: `Builtin::IntToI64 | Builtin::Range | ... | Builtin::Max => {}`. I need to add `Builtin::First | Builtin::Any | Builtin::All` there.\n\nAnd the `expr` arms after `Max`.\n\nLet me also check the import gating: `uses(\"tlMax(\") => &[\"cmp\"]`. `tlFirst` uses `[T any]` so no `cmp` import. `tlAny`/`tlAll` use `[]bool` so no `cmp`. So no new imports needed. Good.\n\nLet me add the Go helper consts after MAX_HELPER.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0688df9f1001leWezBhXivuH9r","sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","messageID":"msg_0688dd4d9001Dv3SpjRJpr0i7l"}}
