emitted in LLVM to see if there's a zext for bool elements. Let me grep for how the map body result is stored.\n\nActually, this matters for `any`/`all`: if bools are stored as 0/1 i64, then `any` = \"any slot nonzero\" and `all` = \"all slots nonzero\". That's correct for 0/1. But if bools are stored as 0/-1 or something, it'd differ. Let me verify the bool-to-i64 storage convention. Let me look at how a Bool is read/written in the vec columns. Let me search the llvm emitter for `zext` or `bool_type` or how `Vec<Bool>` literals are built.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0688e7f57001a5ptshYXh9ukyD","sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","messageID":"msg_0688e488d001uNagUoQxeQ9ab5"}}
