{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788460587628,"sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-acb8581b61d907dd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_llvm.rs","limit":30,"offset":975},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_llvm.rs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n975:             // The checker refuses a program whose result contains a stream, since there is\n976:             // nothing to print: a stream has no value, only a promise that collect can redeem.\n977:             Type::Stream(_) => unreachable!(\"a stream cannot reach the printer\"),\n978:             Type::Char => unreachable!(\"Char cannot reach the printer, refused by the checker\"),\n979:             Type::Sink => unreachable!(\"a sink only ever prints raw, never through the printer\"),\n980:             Type::Str => self.call_rt(self.rt.quote, &[value], \"quoted\")?,\n981:             // tl_int_to_str already takes the full i64, so both widths print through it.\n982:             Type::Int | Type::Int64 => self.call_rt(self.rt.int_to_str, &[value], \"int_str\")?,\n983:             Type::Float => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),\n984:             Type::Bool => {\n985:                 let t = self.string_const(\"true\");\n986:                 let f = self.string_const(\"false\");\n987:                 self.builder\n988:                     .build_select(value.into_int_value(), t, f, \"bool_str\")\n989:                     .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n990:             }\n991:             Type::Vec(elem) => self.join_shown(value, elem, \"[\", \",\", \"]\")?,\n992:             // Absence needs a branch rather than a select, because rendering what is present\n993:             // may itself emit a loop, and a select would evaluate both sides.\n994:             Type::Enum { .. } if ty.as_opt().is_some() => {\n995:                 let inner = ty.as_opt().expect(\"guarded\");\n996:                 let function = self\n997:                     .builder\n998:                     .get_insert_block()\n999:                     .and_then(|b| b.get_parent())\n1000:                     .ok_or(\"no function to branch in\")?;\n1001:                 let ptr_ty = self.ctx.ptr_type(AddressSpace::default());\n1002:                 let slot = self\n1003:                     .builder\n1004:                     .build_alloca(ptr_ty, \"shown\")\n\n(Showing lines 975-1004 of 2664. Use offset=1005 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"            // The checker refuses a program whose result contains a stream, since there is\n            // nothing to print: a stream has no value, only a promise that collect can redeem.\n            Type::Stream(_) => unreachable!(\"a stream cannot reach the printer\"),\n            Type::Char => unreachable!(\"Char cannot reach the printer, refused by the checker\"),\n            Type::Sink => unreachable!(\"a sink only ever prints raw, never through the printer\"),\n            Type::Str => self.call_rt(self.rt.quote, &[value], \"quoted\")?,\n            // tl_int_to_str already takes the full i64, so both widths print through it.\n            Type::Int | Type::Int64 => self.call_rt(self.rt.int_to_str, &[value], \"int_str\")?,\n            Type::Float => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),\n            Type::Bool => {\n                let t = self.string_const(\"true\");\n                let f = self.string_const(\"false\");\n                self.builder\n                    .build_select(value.into_int_value(), t, f, \"bool_str\")\n                    .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n            }\n            Type::Vec(elem) => self.join_shown(value, elem, \"[\", \",\", \"]\")?,\n            // Absence needs a branch rather than a select, because rendering what is present\n            // may itself emit a loop, and a select would evaluate both sides.\n            Type::Enum { .. } if ty.as_opt().is_some() => {","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_llvm.rs","text":"            // The checker refuses a program whose result contains a stream, since there is\n            // nothing to print: a stream has no value, only a promise that collect can redeem.\n            Type::Stream(_) => unreachable!(\"a stream cannot reach the printer\"),\n            Type::Char => unreachable!(\"Char cannot reach the printer, refused by the checker\"),\n            Type::Sink => unreachable!(\"a sink only ever prints raw, never through the printer\"),\n            Type::Str => self.call_rt(self.rt.quote, &[value], \"quoted\")?,\n            // tl_int_to_str already takes the full i64, so both widths print through it.\n            Type::Int | Type::Int64 => self.call_rt(self.rt.int_to_str, &[value], \"int_str\")?,\n            Type::Float => unreachable!(\"Float is JS-only in this row\"),\n            Type::Bool => {\n                let t = self.string_const(\"true\");\n                let f = self.string_const(\"false\");\n                self.builder\n                    .build_select(value.into_int_value(), t, f, \"bool_str\")\n                    .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n            }\n            Type::Vec(elem) => self.join_shown(value, elem, \"[\", \",\", \"]\")?,\n            // Absence needs a branch rather than a select, because rendering what is present\n            // may itself emit a loop, and a select would evaluate both sides.\n            Type::Enum { .. } if ty.as_opt().is_some() => {\n                let inner = ty.as_opt().expect(\"guarded\");\n                let function = self\n                    .builder\n                    .get_insert_block()\n                    .and_then(|b| b.get_parent())\n                    .ok_or(\"no function to branch in\")?;\n                let ptr_ty = self.ctx.ptr_type(AddressSpace::default());\n                let slot = self\n                    .builder\n                    .build_alloca(ptr_ty, \"shown\")","lineStart":975,"lineEnd":1004,"totalLines":2664,"truncated":true}},"title":"src/emit_llvm.rs","time":{"start":1788460587613,"end":1788460587626}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"The `is_record` flag in `Kind::Index` is precomputed by the checker (`elem_is_record` field). For `first`, I need to compute `is_record` from the element type at emit time. Let me check: `arg.ty.elem()` gives the element type; `is_record = matches!(elem, Type::Record(_))`.\n\nFor the LLVM `first` arm, I'll add a dedicated C function `tl_vec_first(const tl_vec *v, int is_record)`:\n```c\nint64_t *tl_vec_first(const tl_vec *v, int is_record) {\n    if (v->len == 0) return NULL;\n    return tl_opt_some(is_record ? (int64_t)tl_rec_from_vec(v, 0) : v->cols[0][0]);\n}\n```\nAnd declare it in `Runtime` as `vec_first: FunctionValue`, add to `new`: `vec_first: module.add_function(\"tl_vec_first\", ptr.fn_type(&[ptr.into(), i32t.into()], false), None)`.\n\nFor `any`/`all`:\n```c\nint64_t tl_vec_any(const tl_vec *v) {\n    for (int64_t i = 0; i < v->len; i++) {\n        if (v->cols[0][i]) return 1;\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\nint64_t tl_vec_all(const tl_vec *v) {\n    for (int64_t i = 0; i < v->len; i++) {\n        if (!v->cols[0][i]) return 0;\n    }\n    return 1;\n}\n```\nThese return i64 (0/1), matching the Bool representation (i64 0/1). The result type is Bool which the llvm emitter reads as i1. Let me check how `Builtin::Max` (returns `Opt<T>`, a pointer) handles the result -- it returns a pointer (`ptr.fn_type`). For `any`/`all`, the result is `Bool` (i1), but the C function returns i64. Let me check how a Bool-resulting builtin or expression is handled. The `vec_sum` returns i64 (`i64t.fn_type`). So `any`/`all` returning i64 is fine; the result is i64 which... wait, but the `Tir` for `any` has type `Bool`, and `llvm_type(Bool)` = `i1`. But the C function returns i64. There's a mismatch: the emitted value is i64 but the type says i1.\n\nLet me check how `vec_sum` (which returns `Int` = i64) is handled -- `vec_sum` returns i64 and `Int` is i64, so it matches. But `any` returns `Bool` = i1, while the C function returns i64. So I'd need to truncate the i64 result to i1. Hmm.\n\nActually, let me check how comparison results (which are i1) flow when stored. And how a top-level Bool result is printed. The `show`/printer for Bool... Let me check how a Bool value at the top level is shown. Actually, let me reconsider: maybe I should make `tl_vec_any`/`tl_vec_all` return i64 (0/1) and then the emitter truncates to i1, OR I keep the result as i64 and handle the truncation.\n\nWait, how does the LLVM emitter handle a `Logic` (and/or) which produces i1? And how does it handle the result when it's a value? Let me check how `Kind::Logic` is emitted and whether the result is i1. And how a top-level Bool is printed (the `show` function).\n\nActually, the simplest approach: make `tl_vec_any`/`tl_vec_all` return `int` (which is i32 in C, but the LLVM decl would be i32). Hmm, but that complicates. Let me look at how the existing `Compare` (i1) is handled when it's the program's result -- how `show(Bool)` works. Let me look at the printer for Bool and how a Bool value is passed around.\n\nLet me look at how the LLVM emitter handles a Bool-typed expression result -- e.g., does it keep it as i1 or promote to i64? Let me check the `show` for Bool and how `Logic` result flows.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_0688ed951001O1E2GKPeMof65i","sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","messageID":"msg_0688eafae001QqLlY87vcOAj9e"}}
