{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788460602106,"sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-bd24e6dd618f5e73","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_llvm.rs","limit":30,"offset":1768},"output":"<path>/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_llvm.rs</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1768:     fn call_rt(\n1769:         &self,\n1770:         f: FunctionValue<'ctx>,\n1771:         args: &[BasicValueEnum<'ctx>],\n1772:         name: &str,\n1773:     ) -> Result<BasicValueEnum<'ctx>, String> {\n1774:         let args: Vec<_> = args.iter().map(|a| (*a).into()).collect();\n1775:         self.builder\n1776:             .build_call(f, &args, name)\n1777:             .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n1778:             .try_as_basic_value()\n1779:             .basic()\n1780:             .ok_or_else(|| format!(\"{name} returned nothing\"))\n1781:     }\n1782: \n1783:     /// Wrapping 32-bit arithmetic over an i64 representation.\n1784:     ///\n1785:     /// Computing in i64 and then narrowing is what makes this total. `MIN / -1` overflows i32 but\n1786:     /// not i64, so it produces 2^31 and narrows back to MIN, with no branch and no hardware trap\n1787:     /// -- the case that costs C and Rust a check costs nothing here. Only a zero divisor is left,\n1788:     /// and it is the only way arithmetic can fail.\n1789:     fn arith(\n1790:         &mut self,\n1791:         op: BinOp,\n1792:         lhs: IntValue<'ctx>,\n1793:         rhs: IntValue<'ctx>,\n1794:     ) -> Result<BasicValueEnum<'ctx>, String> {\n1795:         if matches!(op, BinOp::Div | BinOp::Rem) {\n1796:             self.trap_if_zero(rhs)?;\n1797:         }\n\n(Showing lines 1768-1797 of 2664. Use offset=1798 to continue.)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"    fn call_rt(\n        &self,\n        f: FunctionValue<'ctx>,\n        args: &[BasicValueEnum<'ctx>],\n        name: &str,\n    ) -> Result<BasicValueEnum<'ctx>, String> {\n        let args: Vec<_> = args.iter().map(|a| (*a).into()).collect();\n        self.builder\n            .build_call(f, &args, name)\n            .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n            .try_as_basic_value()\n            .basic()\n            .ok_or_else(|| format!(\"{name} returned nothing\"))\n    }\n\n    /// Wrapping 32-bit arithmetic over an i64 representation.\n    ///\n    /// Computing in i64 and then narrowing is what makes this total. `MIN / -1` overflows i32 but\n    /// not i64, so it produces 2^31 and narrows back to MIN, with no branch and no hardware trap\n    /// -- the case that costs C and Rust a check costs nothing here. Only a zero divisor is left,","truncated":true,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/src/emit_llvm.rs","text":"    fn call_rt(\n        &self,\n        f: FunctionValue<'ctx>,\n        args: &[BasicValueEnum<'ctx>],\n        name: &str,\n    ) -> Result<BasicValueEnum<'ctx>, String> {\n        let args: Vec<_> = args.iter().map(|a| (*a).into()).collect();\n        self.builder\n            .build_call(f, &args, name)\n            .map_err(|e| e.to_string())?\n            .try_as_basic_value()\n            .basic()\n            .ok_or_else(|| format!(\"{name} returned nothing\"))\n    }\n\n    /// Wrapping 32-bit arithmetic over an i64 representation.\n    ///\n    /// Computing in i64 and then narrowing is what makes this total. `MIN / -1` overflows i32 but\n    /// not i64, so it produces 2^31 and narrows back to MIN, with no branch and no hardware trap\n    /// -- the case that costs C and Rust a check costs nothing here. Only a zero divisor is left,\n    /// and it is the only way arithmetic can fail.\n    fn arith(\n        &mut self,\n        op: BinOp,\n        lhs: IntValue<'ctx>,\n        rhs: IntValue<'ctx>,\n    ) -> Result<BasicValueEnum<'ctx>, String> {\n        if matches!(op, BinOp::Div | BinOp::Rem) {\n            self.trap_if_zero(rhs)?;\n        }","lineStart":1768,"lineEnd":1797,"totalLines":2664,"truncated":true}},"title":"src/emit_llvm.rs","time":{"start":1788460602090,"end":1788460602103}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_0688f121b001WQY2cOakcd9cl6","sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","messageID":"msg_0688f0b39001tYFiRmo8unWsE4"}}
