{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788460641354,"sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"edit","callID":"chatcmpl-tool-a71b2ec55565dedd","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/runtime/toylang.c","newString":"int64_t *tl_vec_max(const tl_vec *v) {\n    if (v->len == 0) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    int64_t m = v->cols[0][0];\n    for (int64_t i = 1; i < v->len; i++) {\n        if (v->cols[0][i] > m) {\n            m = v->cols[0][i];\n        }\n    }\n    return tl_opt_some(m);\n}\n\n/* `first`: the cut operator of the query-is-search model (gh:142). A reified search is a Vec,\n * and `first` commits to the first answer, abandoning the rest. NULL on an empty Vec, the same\n * absence encoding `tl_vec_max` uses. `is_record` decides whether the first entry has to be\n * gathered out of the columns the way `tl_at` does, rather than read straight off `cols[0][0]`. */\nint64_t *tl_vec_first(const tl_vec *v, int is_record) {\n    if (v->len == 0) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    return tl_opt_some(is_record ? (int64_t)tl_rec_from_vec(v, 0) : v->cols[0][0]);\n}\n\n/* `any`/`all`: the existential and universal cuts of the same model, reducing a `Vec<Bool>` (a\n * reified search reduced to a mask of 0/1 slots) to one Bool. `any` is whether the mask is set\n * anywhere, `all` whether it is set everywhere; empty is false for `any`, true for `all` (vacuous,\n * the same answer a reduce starting from the identity gives). Both short-circuit the way the cuts\n * do. */\nint64_t tl_vec_any(const tl_vec *v) {\n    for (int64_t i = 0; i < v->len; i++) {\n        if (v->cols[0][i]) {\n            return 1;\n        }\n    }\n    return 0;\n}\n\nint64_t tl_vec_all(const tl_vec *v) {\n    for (int64_t i = 0; i < v->len; i++) {\n        if (!v->cols[0][i]) {\n            return 0;\n        }\n    }\n    return 1;\n}","oldString":"int64_t *tl_vec_max(const tl_vec *v) {\n    if (v->len == 0) {\n        return NULL;\n    }\n    int64_t m = v->cols[0][0];\n    for (int64_t i = 1; i < v->len; i++) {\n        if (v->cols[0][i] > m) {\n            m = v->cols[0][i];\n        }\n    }\n    return tl_opt_some(m);\n}"},"output":"Edit applied successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics":{},"diff":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/runtime/toylang.c\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/runtime/toylang.c\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/runtime/toylang.c\n@@ -1216,8 +1216,42 @@\n     }\n     return tl_opt_some(m);\n }\n \n+/* `first`: the cut operator of the query-is-search model (gh:142). A reified search is a Vec,\n+ * and `first` commits to the first answer, abandoning the rest. NULL on an empty Vec, the same\n+ * absence encoding `tl_vec_max` uses. `is_record` decides whether the first entry has to be\n+ * gathered out of the columns the way `tl_at` does, rather than read straight off `cols[0][0]`. */\n+int64_t *tl_vec_first(const tl_vec *v, int is_record) {\n+    if (v->len == 0) {\n+        return NULL;\n+    }\n+    return tl_opt_some(is_record ? (int64_t)tl_rec_from_vec(v, 0) : v->cols[0][0]);\n+}\n+\n+/* `any`/`all`: the existential and universal cuts of the same model, reducing a `Vec<Bool>` (a\n+ * reified search reduced to a mask of 0/1 slots) to one Bool. `any` is whether the mask is set\n+ * anywhere, `all` whether it is set everywhere; empty is false for `any`, true for `all` (vacuous,\n+ * the same answer a reduce starting from the identity gives). Both short-circuit the way the cuts\n+ * do. */\n+int64_t tl_vec_any(const tl_vec *v) {\n+    for (int64_t i = 0; i < v->len; i++) {\n+        if (v->cols[0][i]) {\n+            return 1;\n+        }\n+    }\n+    return 0;\n+}\n+\n+int64_t tl_vec_all(const tl_vec *v) {\n+    for (int64_t i = 0; i < v->len; i++) {\n+        if (!v->cols[0][i]) {\n+            return 0;\n+        }\n+    }\n+    return 1;\n+}\n+\n /* Collapse one dimension at `i`, `depth` layers down, counting from the end when negative.\n  *\n  * `is_record` decides whether an entry has to be gathered out of the columns. The column count\n  * cannot stand in for that test: a record with one field has one column exactly like a Vec of\n","filediff":{"file":"/home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/runtime/toylang.c","patch":"Index: /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/runtime/toylang.c\n===================================================================\n--- /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/runtime/toylang.c\n+++ /home/kantord/.local/share/toylang-lanes/issue-search-layer-build/runtime/toylang.c\n@@ -1216,8 +1216,42 @@\n     }\n     return tl_opt_some(m);\n }\n \n+/* `first`: the cut operator of the query-is-search model (gh:142). A reified search is a Vec,\n+ * and `first` commits to the first answer, abandoning the rest. NULL on an empty Vec, the same\n+ * absence encoding `tl_vec_max` uses. `is_record` decides whether the first entry has to be\n+ * gathered out of the columns the way `tl_at` does, rather than read straight off `cols[0][0]`. */\n+int64_t *tl_vec_first(const tl_vec *v, int is_record) {\n+    if (v->len == 0) {\n+        return NULL;\n+    }\n+    return tl_opt_some(is_record ? (int64_t)tl_rec_from_vec(v, 0) : v->cols[0][0]);\n+}\n+\n+/* `any`/`all`: the existential and universal cuts of the same model, reducing a `Vec<Bool>` (a\n+ * reified search reduced to a mask of 0/1 slots) to one Bool. `any` is whether the mask is set\n+ * anywhere, `all` whether it is set everywhere; empty is false for `any`, true for `all` (vacuous,\n+ * the same answer a reduce starting from the identity gives). Both short-circuit the way the cuts\n+ * do. */\n+int64_t tl_vec_any(const tl_vec *v) {\n+    for (int64_t i = 0; i < v->len; i++) {\n+        if (v->cols[0][i]) {\n+            return 1;\n+        }\n+    }\n+    return 0;\n+}\n+\n+int64_t tl_vec_all(const tl_vec *v) {\n+    for (int64_t i = 0; i < v->len; i++) {\n+        if (!v->cols[0][i]) {\n+            return 0;\n+        }\n+    }\n+    return 1;\n+}\n+\n /* Collapse one dimension at `i`, `depth` layers down, counting from the end when negative.\n  *\n  * `is_record` decides whether an entry has to be gathered out of the columns. The column count\n  * cannot stand in for that test: a record with one field has one column exactly like a Vec of\n","additions":34,"deletions":0},"truncated":false},"title":"runtime/toylang.c","time":{"start":1788460641351,"end":1788460641353}},"metadata":{"openrouter":{"reasoning_details":[]}},"id":"prt_0688f9cff001X2DeL4fJ1K8GVv","sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","messageID":"msg_0688f9625001HDklvikiliGl9l"}}
