docs pages.\n- `tag_corpus` -- regenerates node_types.\n- The backend-specific snapshot tests.\n- The step_*.rs tests.\n\nThis will be slow (cold worktree, LLVM compile). Let me run it with a long timeout. The brief says \"a cold worktree compiles first -- give it time, never abort it\". Let me run with a 600s timeout.\n\nBut wait -- `cargo nextest run` requires `cargo-nextest` to be installed. Let me check. The justfile uses it, so it should be installed. Let me run `just check`.\n\nActually, before running the full `just check`, let me run a quick `cargo test --no-run` to catch compile errors in the test files, and run the tag_corpus + a single corpus shard. Actually, let me just run `just check` and see. Let me give it a long timeout.\n\nHmm, the concern: the LLVM backend test (`backend_llvm.rs`) compiles and runs native binaries, which needs `cc`. And the corpus harness runs all 7 backends including native (LLVM) which compiles C. This could be slow. Let me run with 600s timeout.\n\nActually, let me first just run `cargo nextest run -E 'not test(every_fragment_is_a_real_program)'` but maybe filter to just my new tests first to iterate fast. Let me run the tag_corpus test first (it regenerates node_types), then a corpus shard.\n\nLet me run `cargo nextest run -E 'test(tag_the_corpus)'` first to regenerate node_types, then check compile.\n\nActually, let me just run the full `just check` -- it's the prescribed loop and the brief says give it time. Let me run it.","format":"unknown","index":0}]}},"id":"prt_068927418001g953CqzTq6M7jn","sessionID":"ses_f977bc931ffe9OHrIOJvOWQPwa","messageID":"msg_06892563b001rbSkA2aSLuU8Dr"}}
